// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// ---------------------
// This is a VS Code IDE-only file. Node.js, npm, and all build tools ignore it completely.
//
// VS Code ships a built-in TypeScript Language Service (tsserver) that activates on ALL
// JavaScript files — including extensionless scripts with a "#!/usr/bin/env node" shebang.
// Without this file, tsserver treats every file it opens here as part of an "implicit project"
// and reports false-positive errors (e.g. on JSDoc comments, import statements in
// extensionless files, etc.).
//
// This jsconfig.json creates an EXPLICIT project root for this directory, which:
//   1. Prevents tsserver from inheriting workspace-level implicit-project defaults
//   2. Sets checkJs:false so the TS type-checker is silent on plain JS files
//   3. Declares NodeNext module resolution so ESM import/export in extensionless
//      scripts (gitlab-search-blobs, gitlab-search-all-projects) is understood correctly
//
// The scripts here are intentionally extensionless so they can be any language in future.
// This file only affects what VS Code shows in the Problems panel — nothing else.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "checkJs": false,
    "noEmit": true
  }
}
